  "title": "Bump jsonschema 0.30 → 0.58 in the osf CLI",
  "summary": "Upgrades the `jsonschema` crate used by the `osf` crate from 0.30.0 to 0.58.6 and adapts the one call site in `answer.rs` to the new accessor API (`error.kind()` and `error.instance_path()` instead of public fields). The rest of the diff is the transitive dependency churn in `Cargo.lock`: the validator now pulls in `jsonschema-regex`/`jsonschema-value`, `referencing` 0.58, `fancy-regex` 0.19, `fraction` 0.17, and drops `futures-util`, `uuid`, and the old `base64 0.22`. No behavior is intended to change — schema validation still produces the same human-readable reason strings.",
